      <div type="clause" n="Inscr.">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIIEg">III Eg</ref> Inscr.</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="Inscr." corresp="#wit-d">Eadgares cynincges gerædnes.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d">Eadgares cynincges gerædnes</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d">King Edgar's ordinance.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">(König Eadgars [Weltliche Ld] Verordnung. D)</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(King Edgar's [secular, Ld] ordinance. D)</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Heading only in D (not original). Base text K = G (Cotton Nero A I); N = A (Harley 55); D is also given here. A second copy, G2 (Nero A I f. 89, c. 1060, a different hand and originally a different manuscript), begins in the middle of III Eg 3 after lost leaves.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
